    "cause": "tokio::join! finishes both server and request. status? returns its concrete RequestError first; an already-completed presented_to_origin Err is then dropped before proxy cleanup. finish_certificate_proxy preserves proxy failure but cannot recover this discarded origin result.",
    "contract": "Explicit operation cleanup must retain completed relevant sibling failures together with client primary and proxy outcomes.",
    "minimal_remedy": "Map successful request/origin results through unchanged literal status/certificate assertions, combine both Result values with existing finish_with_cleanup, then continue the existing gate/proxy cleanup. Add bounded controls sharing these canonical caller result paths; preserve all original assertions.",
    "evidence_class": "source-confirmed simultaneous-result branch; no new native reproduction"
  },
  "approved_scopes": [
    "Missing-certificate classifier now requires actual SSL library16/reason192 for TCP and actual QUIC CertificateRequired crypto code, plus existing client error category. Wrong-certificate and successful server results do not satisfy those helper predicates.",
    "Both WSS clients/profiles and both HTTPS proxy builders/acceptors are prepared before spawning. ConnectionPeer eagerly owns acquired tasks. Original client bindings remain alive through explicit stop/join or returned EstablishedTunnel.cancel.",
    "WSS cleanup preserves completed PeerFailure and main PrimaryFailure with existing FixtureFailures. HTTPS finish observes already-completed proxy Result and, if successful, returned relay cancellation. stop is bounded5s, parent wait10s; only intentional cancelled JoinError is accepted.",
    "No new shared API, production TLS/route behavior, broad unrelated error suppression or weakened literal certificate/echo/Close assertion appears in the diff."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Source review is not fixed-native or full-gate approval. Native14eb seven-negative/34-positive context was supplied by integration; this task did not independently review those raw logs.",
    "Drop abort owns cancellation but does not synchronously join or guarantee all running cleanup results. Explicit finish/cancel provides the observed paths described above.",
    "Independent full owner reads expose unchanged sequential-result loss in other ordinary tests and parser helpers; they are not silently declared repaired by this four-caller remedy. The supported blocker is limited to two currently changed canonical callers.",
    "No new resolved BoringSSL/rustls implementation read is claimed here. Concrete classifier code and retained causal controls were read; exact native constant/alert reproduction remains baseline evidence.",
    "Frozen31 source remains untouched; root agreed the finding and assigned a separate regression/remedy follow-up."
  ]
